// D&D's "raises current and max HP by a flat amount for the duration, up to
// 3 creatures" maps onto `IncreaseMaxHealth` (common/src/comp/buff.rs:
// "Raises maximum health. Strength should be the effect to max health.",
// applied as a flat `MaxHealthModifier::Additive`) -- an exact fit for the
// max-HP half. There is no "also heal them for the same amount" primitive
// bundled with it (no double-buff stacking precedent for that combination),
// so the accompanying instant top-up is dropped; the ally only benefits from
// the raised ceiling going forward, the same "ships without the paired
// rider" call this school's own wards make elsewhere (frost_ward.ron's
// dropped retaliation, wardaway.ron's dropped saves).
//
// `targets: InGroup` applies to the whole group in aura range, not capped to
// 3 -- no per-cast max-target-count field exists on `BasicAura`, the same
// gap protection_from_evil_and_good.ron/shield_of_faith.ron already ship
// with.
BasicAura(
    buildup_duration: 0.5,
    cast_duration: 0.3,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    targets: InGroup,
    auras: [
        (
            kind: IncreaseMaxHealth,
            strength: 25.0,
            duration: Some(28800.0),
            category: Some(Magical),
        ),
    ],
    aura_duration: Some(28800.0),
    range: 9.0,
    energy_cost: 40.0,
    scales_with_combo: false,
    specifier: None,
    meta: (school: Some(Abjuration), source: Some(Divine)),
)
